1. Constraint-Driven Solution Design
Task 1: Determine if String Halves Are Alike
Approach: Count vowels in the first half and second half. If both counts are equal, return true.
class Solution {

    public boolean halvesAreAlike(String s) {

        int mid = s.length() / 2;
        int count1 = 0;
        int count2 = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < mid; i++) {
            if (isVowel(s.charAt(i))) {
                count1++;
            }
        }

        for (int i = mid; i < s.length(); i++) {
            if (isVowel(s.charAt(i))) {
                count2++;
            }
        }

        return count1 == count2;
    }

    private boolean isVowel(char c) {
        return "aeiouAEIOU".indexOf(c) != -1;
    }
}
Example:
Input:  "book"
Output: true
Explanation:
First half  = "bo" → 1 vowel
Second half = "ok" → 1 vowel
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
