7. Matrix Basics
Task 7: Diagonal Difference – HackerRank
Approach
Calculate:
•	Primary diagonal 
•	Secondary diagonal 
Then return their absolute difference.
import java.util.*;

public class Solution {

    public static int diagonalDifference(
            List<List<Integer>> arr) {

        int n = arr.size();

        int primary = 0;
        int secondary = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

            primary += arr.get(i).get(i);

            secondary += arr.get(i).get(n - 1 - i);
        }

        return Math.abs(primary - secondary);
    }
}
Example
11  2   4
 4  5   6
10  8  -12
Primary diagonal:
11 + 5 + (-12) = 4
Secondary diagonal:
4 + 5 + 10 = 19
Difference:
|4 - 19| = 15
Output: 15
