9. Strassen's Matrix Multiplication / Matrix Block Sum
Task 9: Matrix Block Sum – LeetCode
This problem is efficiently solved using a 2D Prefix Sum, which is an important competitive programming pattern.
Java Solution
class Solution {

    public int[][] matrixBlockSum(int[][] mat, int k) {

        int m = mat.length;
        int n = mat[0].length;

        int[][] prefix = new int[m + 1][n + 1];

        // Build prefix sum
        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {

            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {

                prefix[i][j] =
                    mat[i - 1][j - 1]
                    + prefix[i - 1][j]
                    + prefix[i][j - 1]
                    - prefix[i - 1][j - 1];
            }
        }

        int[][] result = new int[m][n];

        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {

            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {

                int r1 = Math.max(0, i - k);
                int c1 = Math.max(0, j - k);

                int r2 = Math.min(m - 1, i + k);
                int c2 = Math.min(n - 1, j + k);

                result[i][j] =
                    prefix[r2 + 1][c2 + 1]
                    - prefix[r1][c2 + 1]
                    - prefix[r2 + 1][c1]
                    + prefix[r1][c1];
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
Important Concept
Instead of calculating the sum of every block repeatedly, we first construct:
2D Prefix Sum
This makes the solution much more efficient.
Time: O(m × n)
Space: O(m × n)
Note: Matrix Block Sum is not itself Strassen's matrix multiplication. It is a prefix-sum problem. Strassen's algorithm is a separate divide-and-conquer matrix multiplication technique.
